{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789218622,"nonce":"3tQEV3VgcPOIfWEaffkfOicJlLo=","title":"drop_insert's alias tracker missed GetElementPtr","message":"derived_values followed a pointer through InsertValue, ExtractValue and\nCast and fell through `_ =\u003e {}`. The struct-literal shape (malloc, gep,\nbitcast, store) left the GEP result untracked, so the store through it\nwas not a use, the last use read as the GEP, and the release went in\nahead of the store. Write-after-free in the shipping pass, latent only\nbecause those shapes escaped by return.\n\nAn unclassified use fails safe (called an escape); an untracked alias\nfails unsafe (released too early). Fixed by walking operands() and a\nnew result_id(), excluding Load and calls, whose results are not\naliases.","files":null}]}